<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · South America</p><h1 class="st-title">State of Maranhão and Piauí</h1><p class="st-meta">1772 CE – 1775 CE · capital São Luís</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A short-lived Portuguese administrative state on Brazil's northern coast, governed from São Luís after the division of Grão-Pará and Maranhão in 1772.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>When the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/state-of-grao-para-and-maranhao">State of Grão-Pará and Maranhão</a> was divided in 1772, the eastern part, made up of the captaincies of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maranhao">Maranhão</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piaui">Piauí</a>, became the State of Maranhão and Piauí, with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sao-luis">São Luís</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maranhao">Maranhão</a> grew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cotton">cotton</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a> for export on plantations worked by enslaved Africans, many imported by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/general-company-of-grao-para-and-maranhao">General Company of Grão-Pará and Maranhão</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sao-luis">São Luís</a> prospered as a port. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piaui">Piauí</a>, with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oeiras-piaui">Oeiras</a>, was a land of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a> ranches supplying meat to the northeast. Little is known of the state's separate administration.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Sources differ on when the separate state was merged back into the general administration of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/new-republic-brazil">Brazil</a>; its captaincies became provinces after 1821. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maranhao">Maranhão</a> stayed loyal to Portugal at independence and joined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazilian-empire">Empire of Brazil</a> only in 1823. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piaui">Piauí</a> and Maranhão are today states of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/state-of-maranhao-and-piaui.jpg" alt="State of Maranhão and Piauí" width="320" height="214"><figcaption>Image: Sodacan This W3C-unspecified vector image was created with Inkscape . · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Portugal_(1750).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1772 CE – 1775 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>colony</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>colonial</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>São Luís</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Roman Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Portuguese</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/brazil">Brazil</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Estado do Maranhão e Piauí</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1774&amp;focus=state-of-maranhao-and-piaui" aria-label="State of Maranhão and Piauí on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="3450 2272 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where State of Maranhão and Piauí lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M3770 2528L3653 2488M3770 2528L3944 2917"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M3653 2488h0M3944 2917h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M3770 2528h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M3770 2528h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks São Luís. <a href="/atlas?year=1774&amp;focus=state-of-maranhao-and-piaui">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
